From 636415e0f216110dfab887bc81cfa9e324177c70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Stackhouse <joseph.stackhouse@stack-tech.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:01:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] expand attention masks on the destination device

Attention masks were uploaded to each card in expanded form on every ubatch.
Across a Gen1 x1 link with no peer path, those bytes are expensive.

This publishes a compact row-visibility hint alongside the mask and
reconstructs the expanded mask on the destination GPU. It removes the upload
rather than compressing it, and covers the sparse-attention block bias as well
as the causal mask.

Default-off, selected by GGML_SCHED_DEVICE_MASK=1. Deterministic output is
retained.
---
